      },
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 2 — Stochastic Gradient Descent\n",
        "\n",
        "**Case Study:** The Boston Housing Dataset  \n",
        "**Algorithm:** Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) for Linear Regression  \n",
        "\n",

      ],
      "id": "f47GlqinlWw3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cz7uB5U7lWw4"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Import Libraries\n"
      ],
      "id": "cz7uB5U7lWw4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "o4ai2qbBlWw4"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_error, r2_score\n",
        "\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10, 6)\n",
        "print('Libraries imported successfully.')"
      ],
      "id": "o4ai2qbBlWw4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8d0TLLWQlWw5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Load the Boston Housing Dataset\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "8d0TLLWQlWw5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "uQCKiB3qlWw5"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "url = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/selva86/datasets/master/BostonHousing.csv'\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Dataset shape:', df.shape)\n",
        "display(df.head())\n",
        "print('\\nColumns:')\n",
        "print(df.columns.tolist())"
      ],
      "id": "uQCKiB3qlWw5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vSQHdG4flWw5"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# The dataset uses 'medv' as the target column.\n",
        "X = df.drop(columns=['medv']).values.astype(float)\n",
        "y = df['medv'].values.astype(float)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Number of samples :', X.shape[0])\n",
        "print('Number of features:', X.shape[1])\n",
        "print('Target mean       :', round(y.mean(), 3))\n",
        "print('Target std        :', round(y.std(), 3))"
      ],
      "id": "vSQHdG4flWw5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hztOfpPTlWw6"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Train/Test Split and Feature Scaling\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "hztOfpPTlWw6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CzS-Odw-lWw6"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
        "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add an intercept column of ones.\n",
        "X_train_b = np.c_[np.ones(X_train_scaled.shape[0]), X_train_scaled]\n",
        "X_test_b = np.c_[np.ones(X_test_scaled.shape[0]), X_test_scaled]\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Training samples:', X_train_b.shape[0])\n",
        "print('Testing samples :', X_test_b.shape[0])"
      ],
      "id": "CzS-Odw-lWw6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cYz5H7J8lWw6"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Stochastic Gradient Descent — Implemented From Scratch\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "cYz5H7J8lWw6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mc2inR1JlWw6"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def stochastic_gradient_descent(X, y, learning_rate=0.001, epochs=100, seed=42):\n",
        "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
        "    n_samples, n_features = X.shape\n",
        "    weights = np.zeros(n_features, dtype=float)\n",
        "    losses = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for epoch in range(epochs):\n",
        "        indices = rng.permutation(n_samples)\n",
        "\n",
        "        for i in indices:\n",
        "            xi = X[i]\n",
        "            yi = y[i]\n",
        "\n",
        "            prediction = np.dot(xi, weights)\n",
        "            error = prediction - yi\n",
        "\n",
        "            # SGD update for MSE (constant factor omitted for simplicity).\n",
        "            weights -= learning_rate * error * xi\n",
        "\n",
        "        epoch_predictions = X @ weights\n",
        "        epoch_loss = np.mean((epoch_predictions - y) ** 2)\n",
        "        losses.append(epoch_loss)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return weights, np.array(losses)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('SGD function created successfully.')"
      ],
      "id": "mc2inR1JlWw6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "90473ZYGlWw7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. One Example Run\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "90473ZYGlWw7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vtWzWbrslWw7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "demo_weights, demo_losses = stochastic_gradient_descent(\n",
        "    X_train_b, y_train, learning_rate=0.001, epochs=100, seed=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "demo_pred = X_test_b @ demo_weights\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Final training MSE:', round(demo_losses[-1], 4))\n",
        "print('Test MSE          :', round(mean_squared_error(y_test, demo_pred), 4))\n",
        "print('Test MAE          :', round(mean_absolute_error(y_test, demo_pred), 4))\n",
        "print('Test R²           :', round(r2_score(y_test, demo_pred), 4))"
      ],
      "id": "vtWzWbrslWw7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AYUG2JvhlWw7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 6. Convergence Behaviour — Example\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "AYUG2JvhlWw7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "U_gJCg22lWw7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure()\n",
        "plt.plot(range(1, len(demo_losses) + 1), demo_losses, linewidth=2)\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Epoch')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Training MSE Loss')\n",
        "plt.title('SGD Convergence — Learning Rate = 0.001, Epochs = 100')\n",
        "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "U_gJCg22lWw7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XoAlDsT7lWw7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Experiment: Epochs × Learning Rates\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "XoAlDsT7lWw7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ufes0hPslWw7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "learning_rates = [0.1, 0.001, 0.0001]\n",
        "epoch_values = [50, 100, 500, 1000]\n",
        "\n",
        "results = []\n",
        "loss_histories = {}\n",
        "weights_store = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for lr in learning_rates:\n",
        "    for epochs in epoch_values:\n",
        "        weights, losses = stochastic_gradient_descent(\n",
        "            X_train_b, y_train,\n",
        "            learning_rate=lr,\n",
        "            epochs=epochs,\n",
        "            seed=42\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        train_pred = X_train_b @ weights\n",
        "        test_pred = X_test_b @ weights\n",
        "\n",
        "        key = (lr, epochs)\n",
        "        loss_histories[key] = losses\n",
        "        weights_store[key] = weights\n",
        "\n",
        "        results.append({\n",
        "            'Learning Rate': lr,\n",
        "            'Epochs': epochs,\n",
        "            'Final Train MSE': np.mean((train_pred - y_train) ** 2),\n",
        "            'Test MSE': mean_squared_error(y_test, test_pred),\n",
        "            'Test MAE': mean_absolute_error(y_test, test_pred),\n",
        "            'Test R2': r2_score(y_test, test_pred)\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
        "results_df = results_df.sort_values(['Learning Rate', 'Epochs']).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "display(results_df.style.format({\n",
        "    'Learning Rate': '{:.4f}',\n",
        "    'Final Train MSE': '{:.4f}',\n",
        "    'Test MSE': '{:.4f}',\n",
        "    'Test MAE': '{:.4f}',\n",
        "    'Test R2': '{:.4f}'\n",
        "}))"
      ],
      "id": "ufes0hPslWw7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HwnDZVKIlWw7"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 8. Compare Convergence for Different Learning Rates\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "HwnDZVKIlWw7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FttfPIAulWw8"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(11, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "for lr in learning_rates:\n",
        "    losses = loss_histories[(lr, 1000)]\n",
        "    plt.plot(range(1, 1001), losses, label=f'Learning rate = {lr}')\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Epoch')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Training MSE Loss')\n",
        "plt.title('SGD Convergence for Different Learning Rates (1000 Epochs)')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "FttfPIAulWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "k-AI-Zl7lWw8"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 9. Compare Epochs for Each Learning Rate\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "id": "k-AI-Zl7lWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JiAPeh7PlWw8"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "for ax, lr in zip(axes, learning_rates):\n",
        "    for epochs in epoch_values:\n",
        "        losses = loss_histories[(lr, epochs)]\n",
        "        ax.plot(range(1, epochs + 1), losses, label=f'{epochs} epochs')\n",
        "    ax.set_title(f'Learning Rate = {lr}')\n",
        "    ax.set_xlabel('Epoch')\n",
        "    ax.set_ylabel('Training MSE')\n",
        "    ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "    ax.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.suptitle('Convergence Behaviour by Learning Rate and Epoch Count', y=1.02)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "JiAPeh7PlWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "YoPRkaDulWw8"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 10. Best Model\n"
      ],
      "id": "YoPRkaDulWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "T1c6YftJlWw8"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "best_row = results_df.loc[results_df['Test MSE'].idxmin()]\n",
        "\n",
        "best_lr = float(best_row['Learning Rate'])\n",
        "best_epochs = int(best_row['Epochs'])\n",
        "best_weights = weights_store[(best_lr, best_epochs)]\n",
        "best_pred = X_test_b @ best_weights\n",
        "\n",
        "print('BEST MODEL')\n",
        "print('Learning Rate:', best_lr)\n",
        "print('Epochs       :', best_epochs)\n",
        "print('Test MSE     :', round(mean_squared_error(y_test, best_pred), 4))\n",
        "print('Test MAE     :', round(mean_absolute_error(y_test, best_pred), 4))\n",
        "print('Test R²      :', round(r2_score(y_test, best_pred), 4))"
      ],
      "id": "T1c6YftJlWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VAu9U7wDlWw8"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 11. Actual vs. Predicted Values for the Best Model"
      ],
      "id": "VAu9U7wDlWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3m_Gm4odlWw8"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
        "plt.scatter(y_test, best_pred, alpha=0.7)\n",
        "min_val = min(y_test.min(), best_pred.min())\n",
        "max_val = max(y_test.max(), best_pred.max())\n",
        "plt.plot([min_val, max_val], [min_val, max_val], linestyle='--', linewidth=2)\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Actual MEDV')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Predicted MEDV')\n",
        "plt.title('Actual vs. Predicted House Prices — Best SGD Model')\n",
        "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "3m_Gm4odlWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "U2GUG0USlWw8"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 12. Automatic Analysis and Interpretation\n"
      ],
      "id": "U2GUG0USlWw8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mZOqiYa2lWw8"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print('=' * 80)\n",
        "print('EXPERIMENT ANALYSIS')\n",
        "print('=' * 80)\n",
        "\n",
        "best = results_df.loc[results_df['Test MSE'].idxmin()]\n",
        "worst = results_df.loc[results_df['Test MSE'].idxmax()]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"1. Best configuration: learning rate = {best['Learning Rate']}, epochs = {int(best['Epochs'])}.\")\n",
        "print(f\"   It achieved Test MSE = {best['Test MSE']:.4f}, Test MAE = {best['Test MAE']:.4f}, and R² = {best['Test R2']:.4f}.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\n2. Worst configuration: learning rate = {worst['Learning Rate']}, epochs = {int(worst['Epochs'])}.\")\n",
        "print(f\"   It achieved Test MSE = {worst['Test MSE']:.4f} and R² = {worst['Test R2']:.4f}.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for lr in learning_rates:\n",
        "    subset = results_df[results_df['Learning Rate'] == lr].sort_values('Epochs')\n",
        "    start_mse = subset.iloc[0]['Test MSE']\n",
        "    end_mse = subset.iloc[-1]['Test MSE']\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n3. Learning rate {lr}: Test MSE changed from {start_mse:.4f} at 50 epochs to {end_mse:.4f} at 1000 epochs.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n4. Interpretation:\")\n",
        "print(\"   • A larger learning rate can converge faster, but if it is too large it may oscillate or become unstable.\")\n",
        "print(\"   • A very small learning rate produces smaller parameter updates, so more epochs are generally needed to reach a good solution.\")\n",
        "print(\"   • Increasing epochs gives SGD more opportunities to improve the model, although improvements eventually become smaller.\")\n",
        "print(\"   • Because SGD uses one randomly selected training example at a time, the loss curve can be noisier than batch gradient descent.\")\n",
        "print(\"   • Standardizing the input features is important because it puts features on comparable scales and improves optimization stability.\")\n",
        "print(\"   • The best configuration should be selected using validation/test performance rather than training loss alone.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n5. Conclusion:\")\n",
        "print(f\"   For this experiment, the configuration with the lowest observed test MSE was learning rate {best['Learning Rate']} with {int(best['Epochs'])} epochs.\")\n",
        "print(\"   Overall, the experiment demonstrates the trade-off between learning rate and number of epochs in Stochastic Gradient Descent.\")"
      ],
      "id": "mZOqiYa2lWw8"
    }
